ListNode* reverseList(ListNode* head) {
    ListNode* prev = nullptr;
    ListNode* curr = head;
    ListNode* next = nullptr;

    while (curr != nullptr) {
        next = curr->next;
        curr->next = prev;
        prev = curr;
        curr = next;
    }

    return prev;
}
```

The `reverseList` function initializes three pointers: `prev`, `curr`, and `next`. It then iterates through the list, reversing the `next` pointers of each node to point to the previous node. Finally, it returns the new head of the reversed list, which is the original tail of the input list."}]

